{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c54ac9cc-408c-4f2b-93e2-10be209ebe2b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ec2955295d6d92a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-0p0bgumj/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E002.md","content":"# Llama Stack API stability guarantee and TP upgrade path\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the API stability guarantee that GA requires for Llama\nStack: the published API surface becomes versioned, carries a deprecation\npolicy, and has a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases. It also\nremediates the API-stability gaps that the GA-readiness assessment identifies\nas must-fix, making the published surface one the platform can commit to\nsupporting.\n\n## Description of inputs\n\nThe scope of hardening work is sized against the GA-readiness assessment (the\ndefinitive GA scope). If that assessment has not landed, this epic's scope is\nan estimate and its content may be rewritten — start this epic after the\nassessment resolves.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Version the published API surface (the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the\n  distribution CRD surface) so GA consumers can pin against a stable version.\n- Define and publish the deprecation policy for the API surface: how breaking\n  changes are signaled, how long deprecated surface remains available, and\n  what consumers must migrate to.\n- Build and verify the upgrade path from the last two TP releases to the GA\n  release, including migration of existing distribution resources.\n- Remediate the API-stability gaps classified as must-fix by the GA-readiness\n  assessment (surface churn, undocumented behavior, breaking changes), or\n  record an explicit deferral with rationale for each.\n- Verify upgrade-path behavior across the supported configuration matrix so\n  the tested upgrade path matches supported configurations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The published API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme is\n  documented where consumers interact with it.\n- A deprecation policy exists and is applied: any existing API surface that\n  will change or disappear under GA is marked with its deprecation path per\n  that policy.\n- The upgrade path from each of the last two TP releases is exercised and\n  passes: an existing TP deployment upgraded to the GA release retains its\n  intended behavior, with any required migration steps documented.\n- Every API-stability gap the GA-readiness assessment classified as must-fix\n  is either remediated in this epic's deliverable or carries a recorded,\n  justified deferral accepted by the strategy owner.\n- Upgrade-path verification evidence exists per supported configuration\n  matrix entry that the support-posture work publishes (each combination\n  tested, or explicitly excluded from support with rationale).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): published API surface carries a stability guarantee — versioned\n  APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP\n  releases. This epic covers that requirement in full, including the\n  assessment-driven API-stability remediation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33796,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd47e305685c09a4","agent_id":"a0c39dc715a16ddec","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"d27fd7b0-ba19-4c30-9a80-6511e9df9ba2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:22:28.746Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
