{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7c00bd06-00ac-4fc4-8f26-cfc3d6dfb9a5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b15a0ee0495853d5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-0p0bgumj/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E003.md","content":"# Llama Stack production support posture\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic puts the production support posture in place that Llama Stack GA\nrequires: documented SLO targets, a backport policy, and a supported\nconfiguration matrix. It also remediates the scale-limit and error-handling\ngaps the GA-readiness assessment classifies as must-fix, so the component is\nsupportable at GA rather than merely feature-complete. The scope of hardening\nis sized against that assessment's definitive GA scope — until it lands, this\nepic's content is an estimate and may be rewritten, so the work starts once\nthe assessment resolves.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define and document SLO targets for the GA distribution (availability and\n  operational objectives the support organization commits to).\n- Define and document the backport policy: which releases receive fixes, for\n  how long, and how security and critical fixes flow to supported releases.\n- Define the supported configuration matrix: the provider, deployment, and\n  scale configurations that are supported at GA, each validated rather than\n  merely asserted.\n- Validate each supported configuration matrix entry with a defined\n  smoke/validation run, so \"supported\" means tested.\n- Remediate the scale-limit and error-handling gaps classified as must-fix by\n  the GA-readiness assessment, or record an explicit deferral with rationale\n  for each.\n- Ensure error handling on the supported surface is consistent and actionable\n  (failures identify the failing resource and the remediation path) for the\n  cases the assessment flags.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- SLO targets are documented and stated in measurable terms, and each has an\n  owner for its measurement.\n- The backport policy is documented and covers every GA-supported release,\n  including security and critical-fix handling.\n- The supported configuration matrix is published, and every matrix entry has\n  a passing validation run recorded against the GA release — entries that\n  cannot be validated are explicitly excluded from support with rationale.\n- Every scale-limit and error-handling gap the GA-readiness assessment\n  classified as must-fix is either remediated in this epic's deliverable or\n  carries a recorded, justified deferral accepted by the strategy owner.\n- Documented scale limits state the observed boundary, not only the intended\n  one, for the limits the assessment examined.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P0): production support posture is in place — documented SLO\n  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. This epic\n  covers that requirement in full, including assessment-driven scale-limit and\n  error-handling remediation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36322,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd47e305685c09a4","agent_id":"a0c39dc715a16ddec","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"e3278230-fc86-4042-813e-d5fcb8535b43","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:22:46.655Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
