in gate remains in the user path for Llama Stack management.\n- Rollback: an administrator can disable Llama Stack management via\n  configuration, and the Dashboard reflects the disabled state — verified as a\n  pass/fail check, since this change replaces the existing opt-in behavior.\n- No stale TP-labeled captions or designations remain on the Llama Stack\n  management surfaces.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P1): the Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate). This epic covers that requirement in\n  full.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36322,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd47e305685c09a4","agent_id":"a0c39dc715a16ddec","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"68a78880-d775-4444-8479-22fa3908e9f8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:23:01.722Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
