{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1bc5c638efcaf13","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n3\tepic_count: 6\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9014: Graduate Llama Stack to General Availability\n11\t\n12\tStrategy status: Refinement Done. Strategy priority: Critical. Triage: full\n13\tdecomposition (not below-threshold — spans three components and three teams, and\n14\tcontains a genuine unknown that gates downstream scope; not docs-only — code\n15\tchanges are required in all three affected components).\n16\t\n17\t## Parsing Notes\n18\t\n19\t- The strategy lists Affected Components as a plain list (Llama Stack, TrustyAI,\n20\t  Dashboard) without per-component change descriptions or owner teams, and has\n21\t  no Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table, Given/When/Then acceptance\n22\t  criteria, or Non-Functional Requirements section. Owner teams were taken from\n23\t  `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/` (RHOAI GenAI for\n24\t  Llama Stack, TrustyAI for TrustyAI, RHOAI Dashboard for Dashboard). Recorded\n25\t  as a health warning; decomposition proceeded with available information.\n26\t- No Staff Engineer Input section is present; no overrides to log.\n27\t- All three affected components have architecture context files, so all are\n28\t  \"in platform\" — no onboarding chain (repo-onboarding / license-validation /\n29\t  konflux-onboarding) is generated. Architecture context confirms Llama Stack is\n30\t  already Konflux-onboarded.\n31\t\n32\t## Epic List\n33\t\n34\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n35\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 | GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E002 | Llama Stack API stability guarantee and TP upgrade path | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E003 | Llama Stack production support posture | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E004 | TrustyAI guardrails as supported Llama Stack integration | Implementation | TrustyAI | P1 |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E005 | Dashboard Llama Stack management enabled by default | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n41\t| RHAISTRAT-9014-E006 | Llama Stack GA documentation uplift and TP migration notes | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n42\t\n43\tE006 priority note: per the docs-authoring priority exception, E006's priority\n44\tis derived from the strategy frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0 (HLR-6\n45\titself is P2; the exception deliberately decouples docs priority from the HLR's\n46\tlevel and from priority inheritance).\n47\t\n48\t## Dependency DAG\n49\t\n50\t```mermaid\n51\tgraph TD\n52\t    E001 --> E002\n53\t    E001 --> E003\n54\t    E001 --> E006\n55\t    E002 --> E006\n56\t    E003 --> E006\n57\t    E004 --> E006\n58\t    E005 --> E006\n59\t```\n60\t\n61\tE004 and E005 are roots (no dependencies); E001 is a root; E006 is the sole\n62\tsink. Critical path: E001 → E002 → E006 (length 3).\n63\t\n64\t## DAG Justification\n65\t\n66\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n67\t|------|------|-----------|\n68\t| E001 → E002 | Investigation edge (Rule 3) | The assessment (HLR-1) produces the definitive GA scope; the size and content of the API-stability/hardening work is unknown until it lands (strategy Open Question 1). True gate: `rewrite`. |\n69\t| E001 → E003 | Investigation edge (Rule 3) | Same assessment gates the support-posture and hardening scope (scale limits, error handling gap remediation). True gate: `rewrite`. |\n70\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 11 (docs last) + content dependency | GA documentation and TP→GA migration notes must reflect the definitive GA scope the assessment produces. |\n71\t| E002 → E006 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation epics — docs describe what was built. |\n72\t| E003 → E006 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n73\t| E004 → E006 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n74\t| E005 → E006 | Rule 11 | Same. |\n75\t| E002 ∥ E003 (no edge) | Rule 15 | Same repo/component, different areas (API versioning & upgrade testing vs. support policy & configuration matrix); no shared build-against artifact. Merge-conflict risk is coordination, not dependency. |\n76\t| E001 ∥ E004, E005 (no edge) | Rule 3 (decision rule) | HLR-4 and HLR-5 are fully specified by their HLRs; the assessment's outcome does not change whether these epics exist or what they deliver, so they are not gated. |\n77\t| E004 ∥ E005 (no edge) | Rule 14 | Different components, different repos, no shared artifacts. |\n78\t| No konflux/onboarding edges | Rule 10 / Step 2 | Llama Stack, TrustyAI, and Dashboard are all in the platform and Konflux-onboarded per architecture context; no onboarding epics exist, so Rules 5–10 ordering constraints do not apply. |\n79\t\n80\tRule 19 (safety-critical strategies) was evaluated and deliberately not\n81\ttriggered: the strategy does not introduce new guardrail, sandboxing, or RBAC\n82\tmechanisms — HLR-4 promotes an already-shipped TrustyAI guardrails integration\n83\tfrom an experimental flag to a supported, documented integration. Fail-mode\n84\tand security validation are folded into E004 as acceptance criteria (defined\n85\tbehavior when the guardrails provider is unavailable; validation on a\n86\tGA-configuration distribution).\n87\t\n88\tThe assessment's outcome is unbounded (an inventory of unknown gaps, not a\n89\tchoice among ≤3 bounded options), so no conditional branch epics are\n90\tgenerated; the gate is modeled as a blocking edge with `rewrite` impact. If\n91\tthe assessment surfaces hardening work that fits neither the API-stability\n92\tepic nor the support-posture epic, that work becomes follow-up scope per the\n93\tassessment's own recommendation (noted in Health Warnings).\n94\t\n95\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n96\t\n97\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n98\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n99\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E001 | GA-readiness assessment producing the definitive GA scope. |\n100\t| HLR-2 | P0 | E002 | Versioned APIs, deprecation policy, tested upgrade path from last two TP releases. |\n101\t| HLR-3 | P0 | E003 | SLO targets, backport policy, supported configuration matrix. |\n102\t| HLR-4 | P1 | E004 | TrustyAI guardrails as supported, documented integration. |\n103\t| HLR-5 | P1 | E005 | Dashboard Llama Stack management on by default for entitled clusters. |\n104\t| HLR-6 | P2 | E006 | GA-standard docs uplift including TP migration notes. Epic priority is P0 via the docs-authoring exception (strategy priority Critical), not via the HLR's P2 level. |\n105\t\n106\tAll six HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements; no HLR is split across\n107\tepics and no epic bundles HLRs at conflicting priority levels except E006,\n108\twhose P0 is the docs-authoring exception, not a bundling decision.\n109\t\n110\t## Component Mapping Notes\n111\t\n112\t- E004's work spans TrustyAI (operator/integration support posture) and the\n113\t  Llama Stack distribution that consumes it. Per the single-most-relevant-name\n114\t  rule it is assigned canonical component `TrustyAI` (the HLR names TrustyAI as\n115\t  the integration surface and the TrustyAI team owns the integration's support\n116\t  posture); the span is noted here.\n117\t- E006 is documentation about Llama Stack GA, assigned canonical component\n118\t  `Llama Stack` with the RHOAI GenAI team (the graduating component's owner)\n119\t  rather than the generic `Documentation` component, so it inherits a known\n120\t  owning team from architecture context.\n121\t\n122\t## Health Warnings\n123\t\n124\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** no Impacted Teams table, no\n125\t  per-component change descriptions, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then\n126\t  acceptance criteria, and no NFRs. Teams were inferred from architecture\n127\t  context; epic acceptance criteria were derived from HLR text. Human review\n128\t  should confirm team assignments.\n129\t- **Unbounded gate (non-blocking):** the GA scope is unknown until the\n130\t  E001 assessment lands (strategy Open Question 1). E002/E003 effort is an\n131\t  estimate until then; any assessment finding that warrants work beyond those\n132\t  two epics should be raised as follow-up epics rather than silently absorbed.\n133\t- **E002 size over the ~2-week guideline:** E002 may exceed the epic guideline\n134\t  once the assessment lands. Kept whole because API versioning, the\n135\t  deprecation policy, and the two-TP-release upgrade-path verification form a\n136\t  single stability commitment over one API surface — splitting them would\n137\t  fragment the guarantee and audit the same API surface twice. Re-split\n138\t  trigger: if the verified upgrade-path matrix (last two TP releases ×\n139\t  supported configuration matrix entries) alone exceeds roughly one sprint of\n140\t  effort, split upgrade-path verification into its own epic gated on the\n141\t  versioning work.\n142\t- **Docs priority surprise (non-blocking):** HLR-6 is P2, but E006 is P0 by\n143\t  the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy priority: Critical).\n144\t  Planners should not read E006's P0 as an instruction to staff documentation\n145\t  ahead of the P1 implementation epics — the DAG still places it last.\n146\t\n147\t## Tiered Delivery\n148\t\n149\tNot applicable: the strategy has no external dependency with uncertain\n150\ttiming. All components are in-platform; no upstream PR/RFC gating is identified\n151\tin the strategy.\n152\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-811b46831ca1b0dc","agent_id":"a7c5c2a6fe8de585d","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"92b190e2-47de-4c55-83cd-5c9a33316971","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:25:01.776Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1bc5c638efcaf13","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
