{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e8adf1cc98520c0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack API stability guarantee and TP upgrade path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the assessment finds the API surface already meets the GA\n15\t    bar, scope narrows to publishing the versioning scheme, deprecation policy, and\n16\t    upgrade-path verification; if it finds deeper instability, scope expands and additional\n17\t    hardening work is raised per the assessment's GA-scope mapping rather than absorbed\n18\t    silently.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Llama Stack API stability guarantee and TP upgrade path\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic delivers the API stability guarantee that GA requires for Llama\n41\tStack: the published API surface becomes versioned, carries a deprecation\n42\tpolicy, and has a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases. It also\n43\tremediates the API-stability gaps that the GA-readiness assessment identifies\n44\tas must-fix, making the published surface one the platform can commit to\n45\tsupporting. The scope of hardening is sized against that assessment's\n46\tdefinitive GA scope — until it lands, this epic's content is an estimate and\n47\tmay be rewritten, so the work starts once the assessment resolves.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Version the published API surface (the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the\n52\t  distribution CRD surface) so GA consumers can pin against a stable version.\n53\t- Define and publish the deprecation policy for the API surface: how breaking\n54\t  changes are signaled, how long deprecated surface remains available, and\n55\t  what consumers must migrate to.\n56\t- Build and verify the upgrade path from the last two TP releases to the GA\n57\t  release, including migration of existing distribution resources.\n58\t- Remediate the API-stability gaps classified as must-fix by the GA-readiness\n59\t  assessment (surface churn, undocumented behavior, breaking changes), or\n60\t  record an explicit deferral with rationale for each.\n61\t- Verify upgrade-path behavior across the supported configuration matrix so\n62\t  the tested upgrade path matches supported configurations.\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- The published API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme is\n67\t  documented where consumers interact with it.\n68\t- A deprecation policy exists and is applied: any existing API surface that\n69\t  will change or disappear under GA is marked with its deprecation path per\n70\t  that policy.\n71\t- The upgrade path from each of the last two TP releases is exercised and\n72\t  passes: an existing TP deployment upgraded to the GA release retains its\n73\t  intended behavior, with any required migration steps documented.\n74\t- Every API-stability gap the GA-readiness assessment classified as must-fix\n75\t  is either remediated in this epic's deliverable or carries a recorded,\n76\t  justified deferral accepted by the strategy owner.\n77\t- Upgrade-path verification evidence exists per supported configuration\n78\t  matrix entry that the support-posture work publishes (each combination\n79\t  tested, or explicitly excluded from support with rationale).\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- HLR-2 (P0): published API surface carries a stability guarantee — versioned\n84\t  APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP\n85\t  releases. This epic covers that requirement in full, including the\n86\t  assessment-driven API-stability remediation.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-811b46831ca1b0dc","agent_id":"a7c5c2a6fe8de585d","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"2be7c44b-fc16-4b6c-8bc7-49201a9d6efb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:25:04.608Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e8adf1cc98520c0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
