{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae4cb3626357a27a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E003\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack production support posture\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the assessment finds no material scale-limit or error-handling\n15\t    gaps, scope narrows to publishing the SLO targets, backport policy, and supported\n16\t    configuration matrix; if it finds must-fix gaps, remediation scope expands per\n17\t    the assessment's GA-scope mapping, potentially as follow-up epics.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Llama Stack production support posture\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic puts the production support posture in place that Llama Stack GA\n40\trequires: documented SLO targets, a backport policy, and a supported\n41\tconfiguration matrix. It also remediates the scale-limit and error-handling\n42\tgaps the GA-readiness assessment classifies as must-fix, so the component is\n43\tsupportable at GA rather than merely feature-complete. The scope of hardening\n44\tis sized against that assessment's definitive GA scope — until it lands, this\n45\tepic's content is an estimate and may be rewritten, so the work starts once\n46\tthe assessment resolves.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Define and document SLO targets for the GA distribution (availability and\n51\t  operational objectives the support organization commits to).\n52\t- Define and document the backport policy: which releases receive fixes, for\n53\t  how long, and how security and critical fixes flow to supported releases.\n54\t- Define the supported configuration matrix: the provider, deployment, and\n55\t  scale configurations that are supported at GA, each validated rather than\n56\t  merely asserted.\n57\t- Validate each supported configuration matrix entry with a defined\n58\t  smoke/validation run, so \"supported\" means tested.\n59\t- Remediate the scale-limit and error-handling gaps classified as must-fix by\n60\t  the GA-readiness assessment, or record an explicit deferral with rationale\n61\t  for each.\n62\t- Ensure error handling on the supported surface is consistent and actionable\n63\t  (failures identify the failing resource and the remediation path) for the\n64\t  cases the assessment flags.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- SLO targets are documented and stated in measurable terms, and each has an\n69\t  owner for its measurement.\n70\t- The backport policy is documented and covers every GA-supported release,\n71\t  including security and critical-fix handling.\n72\t- The supported configuration matrix is published, and every matrix entry has\n73\t  a passing validation run recorded against the GA release — entries that\n74\t  cannot be validated are explicitly excluded from support with rationale.\n75\t- Every scale-limit and error-handling gap the GA-readiness assessment\n76\t  classified as must-fix is either remediated in this epic's deliverable or\n77\t  carries a recorded, justified deferral accepted by the strategy owner.\n78\t- Documented scale limits state the observed boundary, not only the intended\n79\t  one, for the limits the assessment examined.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- HLR-3 (P0): production support posture is in place — documented SLO\n84\t  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. This epic\n85\t  covers that requirement in full, including assessment-driven scale-limit and\n86\t  error-handling remediation.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-811b46831ca1b0dc","agent_id":"a7c5c2a6fe8de585d","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"f9b7febf-9e82-446c-b792-8267328ce1c7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:25:05.433Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae4cb3626357a27a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
