surface, so the\n50\t  default-on change is reversible without a code rollback.\n51\t- Update any captions, labels, or TP designations on the Llama Stack\n52\t  management surfaces that fall out of this change (GA designation replaces TP\n53\t  designations).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- On an entitled cluster with a Llama Stack distribution present, a user sees\n58\t  Llama Stack management in the Dashboard with no opt-in action.\n59\t- On a cluster without the relevant entitlement, Llama Stack management is\n60\t  not enabled by default, and the behavior matches the defined\n61\t  non-entitled state.\n62\t- No TP opt-in gate remains in the user path for Llama Stack management.\n63\t- Rollback: an administrator can disable Llama Stack management via\n64\t  configuration, and the Dashboard reflects the disabled state — verified as a\n65\t  pass/fail check, since this change replaces the existing opt-in behavior.\n66\t- No stale TP-labeled captions or designations remain on the Llama Stack\n67\t  management surfaces.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-5 (P1): the Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n72\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate). This epic covers that requirement in\n73\t  full.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-811b46831ca1b0dc","agent_id":"a7c5c2a6fe8de585d","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"3cb842f0-5b95-4b9b-b26f-0f511e7918a2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:25:08.260Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a76aaaf8a3a852c3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
