{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adbde4f010178587","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# GA-readiness assessment for Llama Stack\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: what separates current\n30\tLlama Stack Tech Preview quality from the General Availability bar. It produces\n31\tthe definitive GA-readiness assessment — a systematic inventory of gaps across\n32\tAPI stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling — and derives\n33\tfrom it the definitive GA scope that all Llama Stack hardening work in this\n34\tstrategy is sized against. The strategy notes that TP feedback is scattered\n35\tacross support tickets and no systematic GA-readiness assessment has been\n36\tdone; this epic is that assessment.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Sweep the sources of TP-era quality feedback (support tickets, issue\n41\t  trackers, release notes, known-issues records) and consolidate them into a\n42\t  single evidence base.\n43\t- Inventory the gaps between current TP quality and the GA bar, per dimension:\n44\t  - API stability (surface churn, undocumented behavior, breaking changes\n45\t    across TP releases)\n46\t  - Upgrade paths (path and friction from prior TP releases)\n47\t  - Scale limits (documented and observed limits under load)\n48\t  - Error handling (coverage, consistency, and actionability of failures)\n49\t- Classify each gap: must-fix for GA, acceptable-with-documentation, or\n50\t  deferred, with severity and the GA-bar delta stated.\n51\t- Produce the definitive GA scope: each must-fix gap mapped to the\n52\t  implementation work that remediates it (within the API-stability work, the\n53\t  support-posture work, or as recommended follow-up epics).\n54\t- State explicitly, for each finding, whether it changes the scope or approach\n55\t  of the API-stability and support-posture work, since those are sized on the\n56\t  current estimate.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- A single assessment document exists that inventories gaps in all four named\n61\t  dimensions (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling), with\n62\t  no dimension left as \"unknown\" without a stated reason and a follow-up\n63\t  action.\n64\t- Every inventory entry carries a classification (must-fix / document /\n65\t  defer), a severity, and the specific GA-bar criterion it fails or meets.\n66\t- The assessment's evidence base is traceable — each gap cites its source\n67\t  (ticket, test result, or measured observation).\n68\t- The assessment produces a definitive GA scope: every must-fix gap is mapped\n69\t  to the work item that remediates it, and the mapping is unambiguous about\n70\t  which existing work stream absorbs it versus which requires new work.\n71\t- Given the assessment's findings, a reviewer can determine, for each finding,\n72\t  whether the API-stability or support-posture work's scope changes — the\n73\t  assessment states this per finding.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (P0): GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between current TP\n78\t  quality and GA bar, producing the definitive GA scope. This epic is that\n79\t  requirement in full.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-915a50155c309142","agent_id":"a6560e1440556b2e9","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"6e71adcd-49a1-4728-a18e-ede53418a8ae","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:30:25.548Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-adbde4f010178587","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
