{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0617647ce07c6be","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack API stability guarantee and TP upgrade path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the assessment finds the API surface already meets the GA\n16\t    bar, scope narrows to publishing the versioning scheme, deprecation policy, and\n17\t    upgrade-path verification; if it finds deeper instability, scope expands and additional\n18\t    hardening work is raised per the assessment's GA-scope mapping rather than absorbed\n19\t    silently.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: Medium\n33\tai_implementability_score: 2\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Llama Stack API stability guarantee and TP upgrade path\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tThis epic delivers the API stability guarantee that GA requires for Llama\n42\tStack: the published API surface becomes versioned, carries a deprecation\n43\tpolicy, and has a tested upgrade path from the last two TP releases. It also\n44\tremediates the API-stability gaps that the GA-readiness assessment identifies\n45\tas must-fix, making the published surface one the platform can commit to\n46\tsupporting. The scope of hardening is sized against that assessment's\n47\tdefinitive GA scope — until it lands, this epic's content is an estimate and\n48\tmay be rewritten, so the work starts once the assessment resolves. The\n49\tupgrade-path verification in this epic's scope is evaluated against the\n50\tsupported configuration matrix that the production support-posture work\n51\tpublishes, so that work lands before the verification completes.\n52\t\n53\t## Scope\n54\t\n55\t- Version the published API surface (the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs and the\n56\t  distribution CRD surface) so GA consumers can pin against a stable version.\n57\t- Define and publish the deprecation policy for the API surface: how breaking\n58\t  changes are signaled, how long deprecated surface remains available, and\n59\t  what consumers must migrate to.\n60\t- Build and verify the upgrade path from the last two TP releases to the GA\n61\t  release, including migration of existing distribution resources.\n62\t- Remediate the API-stability gaps classified as must-fix by the GA-readiness\n63\t  assessment (surface churn, undocumented behavior, breaking changes), or\n64\t  record an explicit deferral with rationale for each.\n65\t- Verify upgrade-path behavior across the supported configuration matrix so\n66\t  the tested upgrade path matches supported configurations.\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- The published API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme is\n71\t  documented where consumers interact with it.\n72\t- A deprecation policy exists and is applied: any existing API surface that\n73\t  will change or disappear under GA is marked with its deprecation path per\n74\t  that policy.\n75\t- The upgrade path from each of the last two TP releases is exercised and\n76\t  passes: an existing TP deployment upgraded to the GA release retains its\n77\t  intended behavior, with any required migration steps documented.\n78\t- Every API-stability gap the GA-readiness assessment classified as must-fix\n79\t  is either remediated in this epic's deliverable or carries a recorded,\n80\t  justified deferral accepted by the strategy owner.\n81\t- Upgrade-path verification evidence exists per supported configuration\n82\t  matrix entry that the support-posture work publishes (each combination\n83\t  tested, or explicitly excluded from support with rationale).\n84\t\n85\t## HLR Traceability\n86\t\n87\t- HLR-2 (P0): published API surface carries a stability guarantee — versioned\n88\t  APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last two TP\n89\t  releases. This epic covers that requirement in full, including the\n90\t  assessment-driven API-stability remediation.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-915a50155c309142","agent_id":"a6560e1440556b2e9","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"807f97e5-c5bc-4a53-873d-9a62ffe87403","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:30:26.166Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0617647ce07c6be","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
