{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac91838976927386","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n3\ttitle: TrustyAI guardrails as supported Llama Stack integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# TrustyAI guardrails as supported Llama Stack integration\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic promotes the TrustyAI safety-guardrails integration for Llama Stack\n34\tdistributions from an experimental flag to a supported, documented\n35\tintegration, as GA distributions require. The integration already exists\n36\tbehind an experimental opt-in; this epic makes it a first-class supported\n37\tsurface: validated on GA configurations, safe in its failure modes, and\n38\tdocumented for users. The work spans the TrustyAI operator/integration side\n39\tand the Llama Stack distribution configuration that consumes it; the TrustyAI\n40\tteam owns the integration's support posture.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Remove the experimental gating so the TrustyAI guardrails integration is a\n45\t  supported configuration for GA Llama Stack distributions (not an\n46\t  experimental flag).\n47\t- Validate the integration end-to-end on a GA-configuration distribution:\n48\t  guardrails requests flow between the Llama Stack distribution and the\n49\t  TrustyAI service and are enforced as configured. Here a GA-configuration\n50\t  distribution means one deployed with the GA release's supported provider\n51\t  and deployment configuration (the distribution CRD's supported surface for\n52\t  that release) — a property of the release under validation, defined\n53\t  independently of the enumerated supported configuration matrix that the\n54\t  production support-posture work publishes in parallel.\n55\t- Define and validate fail-mode behavior: what happens to requests and to the\n56\t  distribution when the guardrails provider is unavailable or misconfigured,\n57\t  with the degradation explicit rather than emergent.\n58\t- Document the supported integration: supported configuration, setup, and\n59\t  behavior, including the fail-mode behavior above, as user-facing\n60\t  documentation for the integration.\n61\t- Confirm the supported designation with the support posture it implies\n62\t  (where users report issues, what is covered).\n63\t\n64\t## Acceptance Criteria\n65\t\n66\t- On a GA-configuration Llama Stack distribution with TrustyAI deployed, the\n67\t  guardrails integration works without any experimental opt-in flag, and a\n68\t  request subject to a configured guardrail is handled per that guardrail.\n69\t- Fail-mode behavior is defined, implemented, and verified: with the\n70\t  guardrails provider unavailable, the distribution behaves per the documented\n71\t  policy (e.g., fail closed or open per configuration) — not with an undefined\n72\t  error.\n73\t- The integration is documented end-to-end (configuration, setup, behavior,\n74\t  fail-mode), and the documentation matches the validated behavior.\n75\t- The experimental flag (or its equivalent gating) is removed or retired such\n76\t  that no user action is required to reach the supported configuration.\n77\t- Misconfiguration produces an actionable error identifying the misconfigured\n78\t  resource.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- HLR-4 (P1): safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n83\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. This epic\n84\t  covers that requirement in full.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-915a50155c309142","agent_id":"a6560e1440556b2e9","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"45e386ea-54e6-47d7-b72a-e6de0fb5029c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:30:27.443Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac91838976927386","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
