{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-811fba5c50a67d58","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E005\n3\ttitle: Dashboard Llama Stack management enabled by default\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Dashboard Llama Stack management enabled by default\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes the Dashboard's Llama Stack management capability available by\n34\tdefault for entitled clusters, removing the Tech Preview opt-in gate. Today\n35\tusers must opt in to see Llama Stack management in the Dashboard; at GA the\n36\tcapability is simply present for entitled clusters. Because this changes\n37\tdefault user-facing behavior, it ships with a rollback path.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Enable the Llama Stack management sections (navigation, resource views, and\n42\t  management surfaces for Llama Stack distributions) by default for entitled\n43\t  clusters, removing the TP opt-in gate from the user path.\n44\t- Define and implement the non-entitled behavior: clusters without the\n45\t  relevant entitlement do not get the capability surfaced (or see the defined\n46\t  not-entitled state), matching entitlement behavior for other GA\n47\t  capabilities.\n48\t- Retain a configuration-level rollback: administrators can disable Llama\n49\t  Stack management via the Dashboard's configuration surface, so the\n50\t  default-on change is reversible without a code rollback.\n51\t- Update any captions, labels, or TP designations on the Llama Stack\n52\t  management surfaces that fall out of this change (GA designation replaces TP\n53\t  designations).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- On an entitled cluster with a Llama Stack distribution present, a user sees\n58\t  Llama Stack management in the Dashboard with no opt-in action.\n59\t- On a cluster without the relevant entitlement, Llama Stack management is\n60\t  not enabled by default, and the behavior matches the defined\n61\t  non-entitled state.\n62\t- No TP opt-in gate remains in the user path for Llama Stack management.\n63\t- Rollback: an administrator can disable Llama Stack management via\n64\t  configuration, and the Dashboard reflects the disabled state — verified as a\n65\t  pass/fail check, since this change replaces the existing opt-in behavior.\n66\t- No stale TP-labeled captions or designations remain on the Llama Stack\n67\t  management surfaces.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-5 (P1): the Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n72\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate). This epic covers that requirement in\n73\t  full.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-915a50155c309142","agent_id":"a6560e1440556b2e9","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"0c222985-a94f-4ef8-860d-5a38db2a34b7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:30:28.407Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-811fba5c50a67d58","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
