{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82ef468c4404ffa1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E006\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack GA documentation uplift and TP migration notes\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E003\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E005\n16\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n17\tgate_failure_impact:\n18\t  action: rewrite\n19\t  fallback_approach: The GA documentation set and migration notes are rewritten to\n20\t    match the definitive GA scope the readiness assessment produces; if the assessment\n21\t    defers capabilities, the documentation marks them accordingly instead of describing\n22\t    them as GA-supported.\n23\tai_signals:\n24\t  change_specificity: 0\n25\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n26\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n27\t  existing_foundation: 1\n28\t  open_questions: 0\n29\t  external_dependency: 0\n30\t  human_process_gates: -1\n31\t  repo_access: 1\n32\t  architecture_claims: 1\n33\tinvestigation_signals: null\n34\tai_implementability: Medium\n35\tai_implementability_score: 2\n36\tjira_key: null\n37\tbranch: null\n38\t---\n39\t# Llama Stack GA documentation uplift and TP migration notes\n40\t\n41\t## Description\n42\t\n43\tThis epic uplifts Llama Stack documentation to GA standards and authors the\n44\tTech Preview to GA migration notes. It runs last: the documentation describes\n45\tthe GA feature set that the implementation work in this strategy actually\n46\tdelivers — the versioned API surface and deprecation policy, the support\n47\tposture (SLOs, backport policy, supported configuration matrix), the supported\n48\tTrustyAI guardrails integration, and default Dashboard enablement — plus the\n49\tdefinitive GA scope the readiness assessment produced.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\tContent outline:\n54\t\n55\t- GA-standard component documentation for Llama Stack: what is supported at\n56\t  GA, the supported configuration matrix as user-facing documentation, and the\n57\t  SLO/backport support commitments in user-facing form.\n58\t- API consumer documentation: the versioned API surface, the deprecation\n59\t  policy, and how consumers pin and migrate.\n60\t- TP-to-GA migration notes: step-by-step migration from the last two TP\n61\t  releases, including distribution resource migration and any behavior\n62\t  changes, aligned with the tested upgrade path.\n63\t- The supported TrustyAI guardrails integration as part of the GA feature\n64\t  documentation (cross-referencing the integration documentation delivered\n65\t  with that work, not duplicating it).\n66\t- Dashboard enablement notes for entitled clusters where the management\n67\t  capability is documented.\n68\t- Removal or correction of TP-era caveats, disclaimers, and \"not for\n69\t  production\" notices that GA supersedes.\n70\t\n71\t## Acceptance Criteria\n72\t\n73\t- GA-standard documentation exists for every GA-supported capability listed\n74\t  in Scope, with no capability documented as experimental that is supported\n75\t  at GA.\n76\t- Migration notes exist for each of the last two TP releases and match the\n77\t  tested upgrade path's actual steps.\n78\t- All TP-era caveats and disclaimers that GA supersedes are removed or\n79\t  corrected across the Llama Stack documentation set.\n80\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented GA\n81\t  capabilities and passes that review — every reviewed statement matches the\n82\t  shipped behavior.\n83\t- The documented support posture (SLOs, backport policy, supported\n84\t  configurations) matches the published support-posture deliverable.\n85\t\n86\t## HLR Traceability\n87\t\n88\t- HLR-6 (P2): documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including migration\n89\t  notes from TP. This epic covers that requirement in full.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-915a50155c309142","agent_id":"a6560e1440556b2e9","session_id":"e9571ff2-2ec2-4b20-9ef4-1431f27af9f3","uuid":"f4f7835f-a8d4-4db5-9903-4c91b4e12b2c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:30:28.865Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-82ef468c4404ffa1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
